    "methodology": "10,000-game solitaire heuristic. Sequencing: land drop, cheapest ramp, commander on affordability, biggest affordable threat, then other proactive spells. Meaningful board = pressure score >= 6 or 2+ threats. Lethal proxy = cumulative combat-pressure proxy >= 40; combat pressure uses mana-value-based creature scoring because card metadata omits power/toughness. Combo lethal = at least one winConditions[] entry tagged kind:'combo' has all pieces present (hand, battlefield, or substitutable by a tutor in hand at +tutor mana cost) and combined mana cost payable. Tutors (cards with primary_role or secondary_role == 'tutor') substitute missing pieces using cheapest-first; tutors and non-permanent combo pieces are reserved from filler casting. Does not model graveyard-piece recovery, token-state combo enablers, or tutor-type restrictions (e.g. Mystical Tutor fetches only instants/sorceries)."
